argon-utils (0.1.41) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Any Argon case may run with or without a UPS, and argond now says
    which at runtime: "no UPS connected" when none is found and none was
    seen before, instead of "no reading yet ... monitoring serial".
  * argond remembers the last UPS it read (/var/lib/argon-utils/ups.seen).
    If that one cannot be found later -- after a reboot or mid-run -- it
    warns once in the journal, shows it in the tray, on the OLED and in
    argonctl ups, and the notification agent announces it. Its return is
    announced as a reconnect, not as mains returning.
  * argonctl ups --forget deletes the record, for a UPS removed on
    purpose; argond stops warning at once.

 -- Simon Keimer <simon.keimer@mailbox.org>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:56:21 +0200

